χός","x":"trochós","p":"trokh-os'","d":"a wheel (as a runner), i.e. (figuratively) a circuit of physical effects","r":"from G5143;","k":"course.","o":"ned.3w.42"},"5165":{"l":"τρύβλιον","x":"trýblion","p":"troob'-lee-on","d":"a bowl","r":"neuter of a presumed derivative of uncertain affinity;","k":"dish.","o":"ikt.1q.1y,j46.2d.2l"},"5166":{"l":"τρυγάω","x":"trygáō","p":"troo-gah'-o","d":"to collect the vintage","r":"from a derivative of τρύγω (to dry) meaning ripe fruit (as if dry);","k":"gather.","o":"jfq.2u.35,nvk.4q.4w,nvl.1j.1r"},"5167":{"l":"τρυγών","x":"trygṓn","p":"troo-gone'","d":"akin to G5149, but denoting a duller sound); a turtle-dove (as cooing)","r":"from τρύζω (to murmur;","k":"turtle-dove.","o":"jad.2j.2u"},"5168":{"l":"τρυμαλιά","x":"trymaliá","p":"troo-mal-ee-ah'","d":"akin to the base of G5134, G5147 and G5176); an orifice, i.e. needle's eye","r":"from a derivative of τρύω (to wear away;","k":"eye.","o":"izp.13.1a,ju9.1i.1l"},"5169":{"l":"τρύπημα","x":"trýpēma","p":"troo'-pay-mah","d":"an aperture, i.e. a needle's eye","r":"from a derivative of the base of G5168;","k":"eye.","o":"icq.1t.20"},"5170":{"l":"Τρύφαινα","x":"Trýphaina","p":"troo'-fahee-nah","d":"luxurious; Tryphæna, a Christian woman","r":"from G5172;","k":"Tryphena.","o":"lvg.7.f"},"5171":{"l":"τρυφάω","x":"trypháō","p":"troo-fah'-o","d":"to indulge in luxury","r":"from G5172;","k":"live in pleasure.","o":"nfb.h.p"},"5172":{"l":"τρυφή","x":"tryphḗ","p":"troo-fay'","d":"effeminacy, i.e. luxury or debauchery","r":"from θρύπτω (to break up or (figuratively) enfeeble, especially the mind and body by indulgence);","k":"delicately, riot.","o":"jgk.3b.3l,njl.2b.2f"},"5173":{"l":"Τρυφῶσα","x":"Tryphōsa","p":"troo-fo'-sah","d":"luxuriating; Tryphosa, a Christian female","r":"from G5172;","k":"Tryphosa.","o":"lvg.k.s"},"5174":{"l":"Τρωάς","x":"Trōás","p":"tro-as'","d":"the Troad (or plain of Troy), i.e. Troas, a place in Asia Minor","r":"from Τρός (a Trojan);","k":"Troas.","o":"l7n.13.18,l7q.n.s,lbj.11.16,lbk.2j.2o,m90.s.x,n23.p.u"},"5175":{"l":"Τρωγύλλιον","x":"Trōgýllion","p":"tro-gool'-lee-on","d":"Trogyllium, a place in Asia Minor","r":"of uncertain derivation;","k":"Trogyllium.","o":"lbt.39.3j"},"5176":{"l":"τρώγω","x":"trṓgō","p":"tro'-go","d":"or perhaps rather of a base of G5167 and G5149 through the idea of a craunching sound; to gnaw or chew, i.e. (generally) to eat","r":"probably strengthened from a collateral form of the base of G5134 and G5147 through the idea of corrosion or wear;","k":"eat.","o":"iij.1a.1q,kav.0.c,kax.0.e,kay.1s.26,kaz.2p.33,kk8.2s.2y"},"5177":{"l":"τυγχάνω","x":"tynchánō","p":"toong-khan'-o","d":"akin to the base of G5088 through the idea of effecting; properly, to affect; or (specially), to hit or light upon (as a mark to be reached), i.e. (transitively) to attain or secure an object or end, or (intransitively) to happen (as if meeting with); but in the latter application only impersonal (with G1487), i.e. perchance; or (present participle) as adjective, usual (as if commonly met with, with G3756, extraordinary), neuter (as adverb) perhaps; or (with another verb) as adverb, by accident (as it were)","r":"probably for an obsolete τύχω (for which the middle voice of another alternate τεύχω (to make ready or bring to pass) is used in certain tenses;","k":"be, chance, enjoy, little, obtain, × refresh…self, + special.","o":"jx2.15.1e,lak.g.n,lff.2k.2p,lhh.0.6,lhh.h.p,lhu.3o.3v,lj1.12.18,m4w.i.k,m6r.2k.2q,m7i.e.i,n0t.1r.1u,n0t.20.26,n82.p.q,nb3.39.3f"},"5178":{"l":"τυμπανίζω","x":"tympanízō","p":"toom-pan-id'-zo","d":"to stretch on an instrument of torture resembling a drum, and thus beat to death","r":"from a derivative of G5180 (meaning a drum, \"tympanum\");","k":"torture.","o":"nb3.1s.20"},"5179":{"l":"τύπος","x":"týpos","p":"too'-pos","d":"a die (as struck), i.e. (by implication) a stamp or scar; by analogy, a shape, i.e. a statue, (figuratively) style or resemblance; specially, a sampler (\"type\"), i.e. a model (for imitation) or instance (for warning)","r":"from G5180;","k":"en-(ex-)ample, fashion, figure, form, manner, pattern, print.","o":"kr0.3j.3o,kr0.4u.4z,kyf.24.2b,kyg.3z.46,lf3.x.13,lnh.3v.41,lo5.2l.2p,m1p.q.y,m1u.18.1h,mpq.2g.2o,mtb.g.p,mwn.1k.1s,myn.19.1g,n2z.w.13,n81.5e.5l,nic.1i.1r"},"5180":{"l":"τύπτω","x":"týptō","p":"toop'-to","d":"to \"thump\", i.e. cudgel or pummel (properly, with a stick or bastinado), but in any case by repeated blows; thus differing from G3817 and G3960, which denote a (usually single) blow with the hand or any instrument, or G4141 with the fist (or a hammer), or G4474 with the palm; as well as from G5177, an accidental collision); by implication, to punish; figuratively, to offend (the conscience)","r":"a primary verb (in a strengthened form);","k":"beat, smite, strike, wound.","o":"iiu.g.o,in3.1b.1g,j65.9.e,jfb.0.p,jog.2f.2m,jtx.2k.2p,k08.14.1a,k1r.2j.2o,l9y.22.26,ldc.3q.3x,leg.1s.1x,leh.z.14,leh.3p.3w,m0r.19.1e"},"5181":{"l":"Τύραννος","x":"Týrannos","p":"too'-ran-nos","d":"a \"tyrant\"; Tyrannus, an Ephesian","r":"a provincial form of the derivative of the base of G2962;","k":"Tyrannus.","o":"lai.57.5f"},"5182":{"l":"τυρβάζω","x":"tyrbázō","p":"toor-bad'-zo","d":"akin to G2351); to make \"turbid\", i.e. disturb","r":"from τύρβη (Latin turba, a crowd;","k":"trouble.","o":"jlo.23.2b"},"5183":{"l":"Τύριος","x":"Týrios","p":"too'-ree-os","d":"a Tyrian, i.e. inhabitant of Tyrus","r":"from G5184;","k":"of Tyre.","o":"l3x.19.1d"},"5184":{"l":"Τύρος","x":"Týros","p":"too'-ros","d":"","r":"of Hebrew origin (H6865): Tyrus (i.e. Tsor), a place in Palestine","k":"Tyre.","o":"i48.39.3d,i49.1b.1j,i92.1k.1o,iqw.25.29,iw7.1j.1n,iwe.14.18,jez.4w.50,jkw.2k.2o,jkx.v.13,lcj.2t.2x,lcn.15.19"},"5185":{"l":"τυφλός","x":"typhlós","p":"toof-los'","d":"opaque (as if smoky), i.e. (by analogy) blind (physically or mentally)","r":"from, G5187;","k":"blind.","o":"i26.16.19,i27.1b.1e,i3s.0.9,i53.1i.1n,i53.30.35,i8v.o.t,i8v.12.1e,i8v.1n.1w,i8v.22.2b,i9b.23.28,i9c.3d.3i,idq.